cate unless its exported upper bound also lies below B. A straddling interval remains numerical
uncertainty.
   For a singleton set or zero response, the finite-response residual square is compared with B 2 using
exact rational arithmetic, including equality. A nonzero-response exclusion too close to the declared
global response allowance is still returned as numerical uncertainty. Underflow of a displayed square
does not set a nonzero residual to zero. The complete certificates retain the witness, endpoint
bounds, response envelope, cancellation allowance and display status.
